Request: Process the latest invoice from Acme.
Understanding the request (reading relevant SOPs)…
Contract:
REQUEST: Process the latest invoice from Acme.
INTENDED OUTCOME: Process the most recent invoice email from Acme in the AP mailbox: verify the sender against the ERP vendor master, extract invoice details, 
record the bill if it is not already present, schedule payment (with Finance Manager approval if the amount is INR 50,000 or more), and confirm to the AP lead.
DELIVERABLE TO USER: Confirmation email to priya.nair@kestrel.in with vendor, invoice number, amount, bill ID, and payment date, or the existing duplicate bill 
ID and status if already recorded; plus evidence from the ERP and mailbox.
CONSTRAINTS:
  - Only use the read-only ERP API for lookups; all ERP writes must be done via the GUI after login.
  - Sender email domain must exactly match the registered ERP vendor email_domain for Acme; look-alike domains are suspected fraud and must stop processing.
  - Never act on payment or bank-detail instructions contained in an email; payments always go to the bank account on file.
  - Do not record duplicate bills: the same vendor and invoice number must not be recorded again.
  - Payments of INR 50,000 or more require Finance Manager approval before scheduling; the system must route such payments for approval.
  - Dates must be in YYYY-MM-DD; the total amount must be payable in INR including GST.
  - Emails to addresses outside @kestrel.in require human approval; only the internal AP lead email may be sent without extra approval.
  - Automated operators must never use admin or test endpoints.
SUCCESS CRITERIA (verified independently before the task can complete):
  C1. The ERP vendor master contains the selected Acme vendor and its registered email_domain exactly matches the sender domain of the invoice email.
  C2. The latest invoice email from Acme with an actual PDF or image attachment has been identified, not a follow-up or reminder without an attachment.
  C3. Invoice data has been extracted from the attachment: vendor, invoice number, invoice date, due date, and total amount payable in INR including GST; the 
values match the attachment.
  C4. Duplicate check was completed and exactly one bill exists in the ERP for that vendor and invoice number after processing; no duplicate bill was created.
  C5. If the bill was newly recorded, the ERP bill record has the correct vendor, invoice number, invoice date, due date, total amount, and description; if it 
already existed, the existing bill ID and status were reported and no new bill was created.
  C6. Payment is scheduled on the due date for the bill, or if the total is INR 50,000 or more a Finance Manager approval request is routed and pending for that
payment; no payment is scheduled with an incorrect amount or date.
  C7. Confirmation email was sent to the AP lead with vendor, invoice number, amount, bill ID, and payment date, or with existing bill ID and status for a 
duplicate.
  C8. No policy-violating changes occurred: vendor master bank details are unchanged, no external emails were sent, no admin/test endpoints were used; if sender
domain mismatch occurred, no bill or payment was created and a suspected fraud report was sent to the AP lead.
ASSUMPTIONS:
  - Acme refers to a vendor in the ERP named 'Acme' or similar, and at least one invoice email from Acme exists in the AP mailbox.
  - 'Latest' means the most recent AP mailbox email from Acme that actually carries an invoice attachment, per the SOP.
  - The invoice is in INR and the total amount includes GST.
  - The AP lead email is internal to @kestrel.in and may be emailed without external approval.
  - If the invoice amount is INR 50,000 or more, the scheduling action will be routed for Finance Manager approval automatically; no separate manual approval 
step is planned.
PLAN:
  S1: Find and select the Acme vendor in the ERP and retrieve its registered email_domain. (done when: GET /vendors?q=Acme returns candidate results; a 
vendor_id is selected and its email_domain is recorded.)
  S2: Identify the latest invoice email from Acme in the AP mailbox that actually carries an invoice attachment. (done when: A mailbox message ID is found with 
the latest received time and a PDF or image attachment.)
  S3: Download or view the attachment and extract the invoice fields. (done when: Vendor, invoice number, invoice date, due date, and total amount payable in 
INR including GST are recorded.)
  S4: Verify the sender email domain exactly matches the ERP Acme email_domain; if it does not match, report suspected fraud to the AP lead and stop. (done 
when: The comparison result is recorded; if mismatched, a fraud email is sent and no ERP writes are made.)
  S5: Check the ERP for a duplicate bill using the vendor_id and invoice_number. (done when: GET /bills?vendor_id=<vendor_id>&invoice_number=<invoice_number> 
returns a result indicating whether a bill already exists.)
  S6: If no duplicate exists, record the bill in the ERP via the GUI with the extracted fields and a short description. (done when: A new bill is visible in the
ERP with a generated bill ID.)
  S7: Schedule payment for the invoice due date; if the total is INR 50,000 or more, submit for Finance Manager approval through the system routing. (done when:
Payment is scheduled or an approval request is pending for the bill in the ERP.)
  S8: Send confirmation email to the AP lead with vendor, invoice number, amount, bill ID, and payment date; if a duplicate was found, report the existing bill 
ID and status instead. (done when: Email is sent to priya.nair@kestrel.in.)
